Cell[TextData[{
 "Each monomial is written as a product of generators, in the order the model \
declares them. The empty monomial is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
 "1"], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"0a19487c-d6e5-4e2f-8a3a-b6a4d4056cbb"],
 "."
}], "Notes",
 CellFrameLabels->{{Inherited, Inherited}, {Inherited, 
    Cell[
     TextData[{
      "26.09.30: Design review - the basis is a list of monomials, each a \
product of generators, because the elements every function of the model takes \
are polynomials in the generators; since Times is orderless a monomial has \
one spelling, and a sign arises only in SullivanModelProduct. The second \
argument is one degree, so an untruncated model with a generator of even \
degree, which is infinite-dimensional, still has a finite basis in each \
degree. The same name gives the basis of a CochainComplexWithPairing, whose \
basis elements are monomials too. Alternative name considered: ModelBasis, \
the name until 2026-09-21, renamed because \"Model\" alone is generic. Prior \
art: the exponent vectors of the monomials of degree k are the solutions of a \
Frobenius equation, which the built-in FrobeniusSolve enumerates, and the \
function keeps those allowed by the odd generators and the truncations. The \
engine the verification suites load lists the same monomials as lists of \
generators, and the suites pin this function against it in degrees 0 to n+2 \
on the catalogue and on Kodaira-Thurston.", "\n\n", 
       Cell[
        BoxData[
         GridBox[{{
            Cell[
             BoxData[
              ButtonBox[
               DynamicBox[
                FEPrivate`FrontEndResource[
                "DocumentationToolsStrings", "Edit"]], BaseStyle -> 
               "TextAnnotationButton"]]], 
            StyleBox[
             RowBox[{
               DynamicBox[
                FEPrivate`FrontEndResource[
                "DocumentationToolsStrings", "LastAnnotator"]], "pavel"}], 
             "TextAnnotator"], 
            Cell[
             BoxData[
              ButtonBox[
               DynamicBox[
                FEPrivate`FrontEndResource[
                "DocumentationToolsStrings", "Delete"]], BaseStyle -> 
               "TextAnnotationRemoveButton"]]], ""}}, 
          GridBoxAlignment -> {
           "Columns" -> {Left, Left, Right, Right}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}}, 
          GridBoxItemSize -> {"Columns" -> {
              Scaled[0.15], 
              Scaled[0.68], 
              Scaled[0.15], 
              Scaled[0.02]}}]]], "\n"}], "TextAnnotation", 
     CellSize -> {590, Inherited}]}},
 CellTags->"TextAnnotation",
 CellID->539496954,ExpressionUUID->"b01c2ce4-73c3-48ad-a016-47237d79626c"],

Cell["\<\
A generator of odd degree occurs at most once in a monomial, and one of even \
degree any number of times.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"59d99154-3763-4d1d-b189-04f1314fd198"],

Cell["\<\
A monomial whose part in a truncated group of generators lies above the \
degree of the truncation is left out.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"c882a6dc-9990-4d1a-b554-ab7bcf7889a7"],

Cell["\<\
The monomials are listed in increasing order of their exponent vectors.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"13f7135e-4762-4eb4-b30b-4d4ec066e34d"],

Cell["The list is empty in a negative degree.", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"19e8026a-b279-4b8b-86a3-3737c42ba5e9"],

Cell["\<\
A model whose generators of even degree are all truncated has finitely many \
monomials. Otherwise there are monomials in infinitely many degrees.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"a66af42e-3551-445d-b9f5-416834860cef"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For a complex, the basis elements of degree ",
 StyleBox["k", "TI"],
 " are listed in the order of the complex."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"a8ef42dc-cb29-4122-b6f9-67f766853b4d"]
}, Open  ]],

